  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Painted Register",
    "overview": "Kabyle and Rif hand-painted pottery, translated to a working screen. The ground is cool kaolin slip; fired-clay red owns the shell (the header rail and the footer, nothing in between); manganese brown-black ink carries text and linework; ochres carry the numbers. Ornament is the potter's frieze: lozenges, sawtooth and hairline rails, drawn as crisp inline SVG, and it appears only where a band means something. Between leaderboard tiers it is the statistical gap made visible, so a change of tier reads as a change of register rather than a rule.\n\nThe surface is a research instrument first. Density is that of a well-set table: hairline rules, tabular figures, generous row height (14px vertical padding), no cards, no shadows, 2px corners. Every score on the site sits on a fixed 0 to 100 scale and is coloured from one stepped ochre ramp, so a colour and a bar length mean the same number on every page. The dark theme is the same pot fired the other way: manganese ground, slip-white ink, the clay deepened and the ochres re-stepped light-on-dark.\n\nTifinagh is treated as a living script, not decoration: it appears as the ⵣ in the wordmark and as single letters of the alphabet, always in Noto Sans Tifinagh with a `lang=\"zgh\"` attribute, never as words.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Clay rail top and bottom, slip ground between; the shell colour never enters content as a fill except in the tier band.",
      "Painted friezes as meaning-bearing dividers only (tier gaps, header hem, footer, one section break).",
      "One ochre sequential ramp for every score; four glaze colours only for comparing named runs.",
      "Flat: hairlines and tonal slip steps, zero shadows.",
      "Archivo variable with width axis; tabular lining figures for every number.",
      "Motion is functional: rows slide in place when re-sorted (260ms), hovers fade in 150ms; reduced motion is honoured."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Shell Rule",
        "body": "Clay fills the header rail, the footer and the tier band, and nothing else. Content surfaces stay slip.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Ramp Rule",
        "body": "Any score, anywhere, takes its colour from the six-bin ochre ramp on a fixed 0 to 100 scale. Never rescale to the data range and never introduce a second sequential palette.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Glaze-for-Identity Rule",
        "body": "Series colours identify a chosen run on the compare page; they never encode magnitude, and the ochre ramp never identifies a run.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every number (scores, intervals, ranks, counts, codepoints) is set with tabular lining figures and right-aligned or fixed-width so columns scan.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Labels-Name-Data Rule",
        "body": "Uppercase label type sits on a table head, field, term or chart axis. It never sits above a page or section headline as a kicker.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Script-as-Letters Rule",
        "body": "Tifinagh appears only as the alphabet's single letters and the ⵣ mark, always in Noto Sans Tifinagh under `lang=\"zgh\"`. No dictionary words, ever (enforced at build by `web/scripts/postbuild.mjs`).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fired-Flat Rule",
        "body": "No box-shadow, drop-shadow or blur on any element. Separation is a hairline, a slip step, or a painted band.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep clay to the header rail, footer and tier band, with slip as the only content ground.",
      "**Do** colour every score from the six-bin ochre ramp with bins at 0, 10, 20, 35, 55, 80, on a fixed 0 to 100 axis.",
      "**Do** show uncertainty wherever a score appears: the interval whisker on bars, `± value` under scores, `=` on tied ranks.",
      "**Do** set every number with tabular lining figures.",
      "**Do** use the painted frieze, tier band and hem as inline SVG at their recorded sizes, only where a band carries meaning.",
      "**Do** keep corners at 2px and separation to hairlines and slip steps.",
      "**Do** give Tifinagh text `lang=\"zgh\"` and the Noto Sans Tifinagh face."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add shadows, blurs or elevated cards; this world is fired flat.",
      "**Don't** use glaze series colours for magnitude or the ochre ramp for identity.",
      "**Don't** put uppercase label type above a headline as a kicker or eyebrow.",
      "**Don't** show dictionary words, model answers or example mistakes, in Tifinagh or any script.",
      "**Don't** draw a tier band in any sort order other than score descending.",
      "**Don't** ship raster ornament or raster icons; ornament, icons and the favicon are SVG, icons on a 20px grid with a 1.6 stroke and round caps.",
      "**Don't** use focus blue for anything but focus."
    ]
  }
}